From 98dc71aa4a7395f9568c852485ac9371f4490826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:36:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cdda: Limit paranoia read-ahead to avoid playback stalls

Playing an audio CD through gvfs, for example in Totem, stops for
about 3 seconds every 16 seconds on a USB drive.

do_read() takes one sector at a time from cdio_paranoia_read(). When
paranoia's buffer is empty, that call first refills its cache from the
drive before it returns, even in the PARANOIA_MODE_DISABLE used here:
normally 1200 sectors, or 16 seconds of audio. A player reading in
real time runs dry while it waits.

Set the cache model to 150 sectors, 2 seconds of audio, as GStreamer's
cdparanoiasrc does for playback. Before 10.2+0.93+1 (2014),
libcdio-paranoia read ahead 150 sectors. That release brought both the
1200-sector cache model and cdio_paranoia_cachemodel_size(), so builds
against older versions are unchanged.

Tested with an ASUS SDRW-08D2S-U USB drive and Totem reading through
gvfsd-fuse, playing a 5:09 track twice per build from a stopped drive.
Without this change, PipeWire logged 19 mid-track underflows of the
player's stream in each run; with it, none. Copying the whole track
took 29.8 s before and 29.0 s after, and the audio was identical to a
direct read with cd-paranoia.

See: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/commit/4e1086f93b509d92529d7af5475e3c9780d201c1
Related: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/1967258
Fixes: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gvfs/-/work_items/893
---
 daemon/gvfsbackendcdda.c | 5 +++++
 meson.build              | 1 +
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/daemon/gvfsbackendcdda.c b/daemon/gvfsbackendcdda.c
index ce01630..cb5f648 100644
--- a/daemon/gvfsbackendcdda.c
+++ b/daemon/gvfsbackendcdda.c
@@ -640,6 +640,11 @@ do_open_for_read (GVfsBackend *backend,
 
   read_handle->paranoia = cdio_paranoia_init (cdda_backend->drive);
   cdio_paranoia_modeset (read_handle->paranoia, PARANOIA_MODE_DISABLE);
+#ifdef HAVE_PARANOIA_CACHEMODEL_SIZE
+  /* Use short refills for playback, as GStreamer's cdparanoiasrc does */
+  cdio_paranoia_cachemodel_size (read_handle->paranoia,
+                                 2 * CDIO_CD_FRAMES_PER_SEC);
+#endif
 
   cdda_backend->num_open_files++;
 
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 1a5b6d4..312d150 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -429,6 +429,7 @@ if enable_cdda
 
   libcdio_paranoia_dep = dependency('libcdio_paranoia', version: '>= 0.78.2')
   config_h.set('HAVE_PARANOIA_NEW_INCLUDES', cc.has_header('cdio/paranoia/paranoia.h', dependencies: libcdio_paranoia_dep))
+  config_h.set('HAVE_PARANOIA_CACHEMODEL_SIZE', cc.has_function('cdio_paranoia_cachemodel_size', prefix: '#include <cdio/paranoia/paranoia.h>', dependencies: libcdio_paranoia_dep))
 
   config_h.set('HAVE_CDDA', enable_cdda)
 endif
